 # Construction Management Data Schema & Template

## Overview
This file outlines the sample data structure used to test and implement our revolutionary construction management framework. By standardizing input data across phases, the system eliminates fragmentation and feeds accurate metrics into the predictive analytics engine.
Sample Data Structure (project_metrics.csv / JSON Schema)
Below is the standard format for tracking milestone execution and resource allocation:

task_id (String): Unique identifier for the construction phase or milestone (e.g., TSK-FOUND-01).

phase_name (String): Broad category of the construction lifecycle (e.g., Foundation & Excavation).

planned_start_date (Date - YYYY-MM-DD): Baseline scheduled start date (e.g., 2026-04-01).

actual_progress (Percentage): Current completion rate verified on-site (e.g., 85%).

risk_coefficient (Float - 0.0 to 1.0): Automated risk score calculated by the predictive engine (e.g., 0.23).

resource_status (String): Status of labor and equipment deployment (e.g., Optimal).

How to Use This Template
Clone or download this repository.

Map your project's milestones into the fields defined above.

Feed the structured data into the framework to initialize real-time tracking and critical path monitoring.
